t(·) and h ̃t(·), and mispecified graph topology (Challenges C.2, C.4). While the error covariance is not explicitly tracked and is not accounted for in the loss (40), it can still be recovered from the KG in some settings [56]. In addition, as the KG is learned without explicit knowledge of the underlying stochasticity, GSP-KalmanNet can learn to track in non-Gaussian noise without knowing its distribution (Challenge C.3). These properties are empirically demonstrated in Section V. Table II details the challenges each benchmark in Section V is facing. Preserving the model-based operation of the GSP-EKF, as done in GSP-KalmanNet, can potentially bring operational gains beyond increased accuracy and reduced complexity. For instance, it was shown in [55], [56] that in some settings one can
